            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.38.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.38.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 38:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Zedekiah replied, “Don't let anyone know about this conversation, and your life will not be in danger. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.38.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.38.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 38:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If the officials hear that I have talked with you, they will come and ask you what we said. They will promise not to put you to death if you tell them everything. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.38.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.38.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 38:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Just tell them you were begging me not to send you back to prison to die there.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.38.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.38.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 38:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then all the officials came and questioned me, and I told them exactly what the king had told me to say. There was nothing else they could do, because no one had overheard the conversation. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.38.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.38.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 38:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EZK.33.21"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ezek 33.21",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And I was kept in the palace courtyard until the day Jerusalem was captured.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.38.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.38.28"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
